  "R0045": {
   "light": "",
   "soundTech": "",
   "action": "",
   "soundCue": "",
   "videoCue": "",
   "klara": "And on that crossroad, there was a shrine. And every day, on the hour when the Earth puts on her grieving clothes for the funeral rites of the sun, an old man brings turnips to the shrine. The god to whom the shrine belonged is an old and tired god, and he cannot help the old man. And he doesn’t much care for turnips. But the old man does not want for much in his life, either. And so, the old god and the old man sit together, every day, for twenty years, on the hour when the Earth puts on her grieving clothes for the funeral rites of the sun.",
   "gary": "",
   "cameron": "",
   "beats": "",
   "notes": "",
   "cut": false
